WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.838
Be clear about where the kits
stop, because an assessor will ask.

2
00:00:03.838 --> 00:00:08.504
Every gate now has a kit check, but most
leave a residual that no check reads,

3
00:00:08.504 --> 00:00:11.412
and the gate names the
evidence that stands in.

4
00:00:11.412 --> 00:00:16.538
For this part, Gate 7's checks cover the
membership change and the counts per code,

5
00:00:16.538 --> 00:00:21.275
but nothing proves the mover workflow
ran, so its own run history stands in.

6
00:00:21.275 --> 00:00:25.149
Gate 8 has its per-wave checks,
but nothing produces the seven-day

7
00:00:25.149 --> 00:00:29.388
sole-source report, so the provisioning
logs joined on the key stand in.

8
00:00:29.388 --> 00:00:33.566
Gate 9 has the HR, group and track
checks, but nothing compares role

9
00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:37.899
assignments with the registry, so
the registry diff in Git stands in.

10
00:00:37.899 --> 00:00:40.088
The earlier gates follow the same pattern.

11
00:00:40.088 --> 00:00:44.174
Sync, Conditional Access and the
PIV binding each have a check now,

12
00:00:44.174 --> 00:00:48.261
but the sync configuration, the
report-only results and whether a

13
00:00:48.261 --> 00:00:52.575
binding belongs to a current card
still come from a report or a record.

14
00:00:52.575 --> 00:00:54.900
Keep this table in the evidence packet.

15
00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:58.660
It shows which gates were proved
by code and which by a record.
